PROMETHEUS & GRAFANA
=======================

These are two different tools

PROMETHEUS
===============

Prometheus in kubernetes is a monitoring tool that helps keep an eye on the health and performance of applications and the overall system running in a 
kubernetes cluster

GRAFANA
=========

Grafana in kubernetes (k8's) is a tool used for creating visual dashboards to monitor and analyze the performance of applications and infrastructure with a 
kubernetes cluster

lets see how to install PROMETHEUS & GRAFANA in our cluster using HELM Charts

STEPS TO SEUP PROMETHEUS & GRAFANA IN KOPS:
==============================================

Install HELM:
==============

HELM
======

Helm is a kubernetes package manager in which the multiple number of YAML files such as the backend, and frontend come under one roof(helm) and deploy using helm.

HELM = Frontend + Backend + Database

helm.sh ------------> this is the official document for HELM (https://helm.sh/)

https://artifacthub.io/ --------> here we can search official documents of what we need like jenkins, promethus, grafana etc

curl -fsSL -o get_helm.sh https://raw.githubusercontent.com/helm/helm/main/scripts/get-helm-4 --------> command to install helm 1st command 
chmod 700 get_helm.sh -------> command to install helm 2nd command 
./get_helm.sh -------> command to install helm 3rd command 

helm version ----------> command to view helm version

Install k8s Metrics Service:
================================

kubectl apply -f https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server/releases/latest/download/components.yaml

verify that the metrics-server depoyment is running the desired number of pods.

kubectl get pods -n kube-system
kubectl get deployment metrics-server -n kube-system

Install prometheus
===================

helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts
helm repo add rafana https://grafana.github.io/helm-charts

Update the HELM Chart Repos:
==============================

helm repo update
helm repo list

Create prometheus Namespace:
=============================

kubectl create namespace prometheus
kubetcl get ns

Install Promethesus
=====================

helm install prometheus prometheus-community/prometheus --namespace prometheus --set alertmanager.persistentVolume.StorageClass="gp2" 
--set server.persistentVolume.storageClass="gp2"

kubectl get pods -n prometheus

kubectl get all -n prometheus

Install Grafana
===================

helm install grafana grafana/grafana --namespace grafana --set persistence.storageClassName="gp2" --set persistence.enabled=true --set adminPassword='EKS!sAWSome' --set service.type=LoadBalancer
helm install grafana grafana/grafana --namespace grafana --create-namespace --set persistence.enabled=false --set service.type=LoadBalancer

